DTSTART:20251213T213000Z
DTEND:20251213T231500Z
DTSTAMP:20251213T213000Z
UID:nyvTtDDqYT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nSIFF Holiday Favorites Charles Di
 ckens’ timeless tale of Ebenezer Scrooge (Michael Caine)\, his cold hear
 t\, and how the Ghosts of Christmas Past\, Present\, and Future seek to sh
 ow him the error of his ways comes to life through the magic of Jim Henson
 ’s Muppets. Recently remastered\, including the original song "When Love
  is Gone." Arrive 30 minutes early for an exciting Muppet pre-show special
 ! All ages welcome ($5 tickets for children aged 2-12 years old\, free for
  under 2).\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/holiday-favorites/t
 he-muppet-christmas-carol\n\nEstimated start: 13:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Singin’ In the Rain (1952)
DTSTART:20251214T200000Z
DTEND:20251214T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20251214T200000Z
UID:kx0LXZNxnL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nSliding Scale Community Screenin
 gs Hollywood’s troubled transition from silent to talking pictures at th
 e end of the 1920s provided the inspiration for perhaps the greatest of mo
 vie musicals\, starring Gene Kelly\, Debbie Reynolds\, and Donald O’Conn
 or. In appreciation of our movie-loving community\, tickets to this screen
 ing are available on a sliding scale basis\, starting at $5 for child tick
 ets. Enjoy the film for less or give more generously to support nonprofit 
 movie magic.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/sliding-scale-com
 munity-screenings/singin-in-the-rain\n\nEstimated start: 12:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
